Write the fractions in eighths.
$\frac{3}{4}=\frac{6}{8}$
$\frac{1}{2}=\frac{4}{8}$
$\frac{1}{8}<\frac{4}{8}<\frac{6}{8}$
$\frac{1}{8}<\frac{1}{2}<\frac{3}{4}$
Divide the interval from $0$ to $1$ into eight equal parts. Mark the first, fourth and sixth division points.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8cm,y=1cm]
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(1.08,0);
\foreach \i in {0,...,8} {\draw[black] ({\i/8},0.08)--({\i/8},-0.08);}
\node[below,text=black] at (0,-0.08) {$0$};
\node[below,text=black] at (1,-0.08) {$1$};
\node[above,text=black] at (0.125,0.08) {$\frac{1}{8}$};
\node[above,text=black] at (0.5,0.08) {$\frac{1}{2}$};
\node[above,text=black] at (0.75,0.08) {$\frac{3}{4}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
